zindorsky <nephi.allred@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Great work. Always fun to have something new to play with. For the
> record, it was pretty easy to compile for Mac OSX and Ubuntu.
>
> Where do we file bug reports?

There's a new "New Ticket" link on the Trac project page:
http://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/unnethack-12312/newticket

> It seems the menu and status color stuff doesn't work on Mac or
> Linux.

The menu and status color stuff must first be configured in the
nethackrc resp. unnethackrc:
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?142
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Menucolors

If it's correctly compiled in it will be shown in #version as "menu
colors via regular expressions"/"menu colors via pmatch".

I didn't have a problem on OSX or Linux (Linux being the main
development OS).

> Also, polymorphed into a gray dragon, the eggs I laid hatched into
> blue dragons (though the eggs were marked gray).

I forgot to shuffle the baby dragons like I do the grown ups at
program start.

> Also, may I suggest integrating some of my enhanced banes patch?
> (http://zindorsky.kundor.org/patches/banes.html)

For the first release I already looked at your patches and some of the
enhanced banes patch has already been implemented, although with
different code.

Banes warn of their favorite enemies and get a chance of canceling
them.

Canceled trolls don't revive anymore. This is extremely nice if happen
to stumble on the troll infested heck level.

> At least the part that changes the x2 damage to +d20. This makes
> them effective without having to spend skill slots and enchant
> weapon scrolls.

I didn't have looked into artifact improving a lot yet.

SporkHack has already done a lot in this respect and I wanted
UnNetHack to go off into a different direction, at least at first.

> If you need any code monkeys, I'd be happy to volunteer some time.

A refactoring of NetHack would be nice ;-) 

You might have seen that your gold dragon patch already got in.

The bags of tricks and the color alchemy patch are likely to be
included one way or the other for 3.5.2.

So I think you already did your code monkey time. :)

